course: dictionary
lesson: 428
title: Arab: a people, a world, a horse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Arab can be a noun or an adjective. As a noun, it names a person: «Chess travelled to Persia, the Arab world and Europe» shows that the Arab world is a place, a group of countries, sitting alongside other places. As an adjective, it describes something, like Arab culture.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. A capital A shows it names a people or a place. In «an Arab horse», the word horse tells you Arab is describing a kind of horse, a breed known for speed and strength. Check by swapping in a meaning: "the Arab world" becomes "the world of Arab countries", and it still makes sense.
explain: Arab names a people and their culture, not a religion. Arabs can follow many different religions. The word tells you where people's families come from, such as the Arabic-speaking countries of the Middle East and North Africa.
fact: An Arab is a person whose people come from the Arabic-speaking countries of the Middle East and North Africa.
fact: Egypt, Saudi Arabia and Morocco are examples of Arab countries.
fact: «The Arab world» means these countries together, with their shared culture.
fact: An Arab horse is a beautiful breed known for speed and strength.
fact: Arab names a people and their culture, not a religion.
exercise: «Chess travelled to Persia, the Arab world and Europe.» In this sentence, the Arab world means | A kind of horse | A chess piece | *A group of countries in the Middle East and North Africa
exercise: «Arab, Persian, Indian and Chinese sailors timed their voyages to the monsoon.» Find and copy the one word that names a people from the Middle East and North Africa. | timed | voyages | *Arab | monsoon
exercise: Ella says an Arab horse is just any horse. What is an Arab horse? | A horse that lives only in London | A wooden toy horse | *A beautiful breed known for speed and strength | A horse with no tail
test: Which of these is an Arab country? | Canada | Japan | Brazil | *Egypt
test: Which statement about the word Arab is true? | It names a religion only | *It names a people and their culture, not a religion | It means a desert | It names a horse only
exam: In «Chess began in India and spread to the Arab world», what does the Arab world mean? | A type of chess piece | A river in Spain | A horse breed | *A region of countries with Arab people and culture
